# Run with an HTTP request client such as VS Code REST Client.
# Start the API first. These requests need no owner cookie.
@api = http://localhost:4000
# Replace with the public key from a site you created in the dashboard.
@siteKey = REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_SITE_KEY
@anon = lessonbrowser001

### 1. API is running: expect 200. This does not check the database.
GET {{api}}/health

### 2. Dashboard requires sign-in: expect 401.
GET {{api}}/v1/sites

### 3. Well-formed but unknown key: expect 404 when the database is reachable.
POST {{api}}/v1/track
Content-Type: application/json

{"key":"000000000000000000000000","anon":"{{anon}}","name":"queue_joined"}

### 4. Extra fields are refused: expect 400 before the database is called.
POST {{api}}/v1/track
Content-Type: application/json

{"key":"000000000000000000000000","anon":"{{anon}}","name":"queue_joined","page":"/private"}

### 5. Real site key: expect 204 with an empty body.
# Sends one test event to the selected site; use a development site.
POST {{api}}/v1/track
Content-Type: application/json

{"key":"{{siteKey}}","anon":"{{anon}}","name":"queue_joined"}

### 6. Wrong method: expect 405.
GET {{api}}/v1/track
